WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.580
Putting it together, the program sorts
every AI system into six kinds of identity:

2
00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:09.873
a delegated assistant,
workload-identity AI, an agent identity,

3
00:00:09.873 --> 00:00:15.238
an agent with its own user account, a
vendor-hosted service, and an unmanaged key.

4
00:00:15.238 --> 00:00:19.003
Each kind tells you who owns
it, how it should authenticate,

5
00:00:19.003 --> 00:00:21.513
what policy can reach it, and how it ends.

6
00:00:21.513 --> 00:00:23.812
Most of the risk sits in the last two.

7
00:00:23.812 --> 00:00:27.787
A vendor's service is visible
but outside your workload policy.

8
00:00:27.787 --> 00:00:30.265
A raw key isn't in the directory at all,

9
00:00:30.265 --> 00:00:33.238
so it has no owner and no
end until you find it.

10
00:00:33.238 --> 00:00:37.150
Everything else can be governed,
and Part 2 does exactly that.
